+# Pickup reminders
+
+For volunteers considering a change to pickup reminders, especially a switch to email to save the SMS cost.
+Reminders go by SMS because an email trial led to more missed pickups and wasted fresh food. This page records why
+SMS was kept after volunteers repeatedly proposed email.
+
+## Channel
+
+The April–June 2025 email trial left 34% of reminder emails unopened, according to the provider's report. Missed
+pickups rose from 6% of pantry orders to 13%. Each missed pickup leaves a packed bag whose fresh food goes in the
+bin by closing time. Many members share one phone in the family and never check email; they see SMS.
+
+The team switched back to SMS on July 1, and missed pickups returned to 6% by August. SMS costs €40 a month, while
+email is free, but the trial showed that saving the SMS fee came at the cost of more missed pickups and food waste.
+The maintainer therefore kept SMS when the proposal came up again; see the [issue 52 discussion](../../notes/issue-52.md).
+
+## Implementation
+
+The reminder channel and sending logic live in [the reminder module](../../larder/reminders.py).
